# AOSP installs android.hardware.boot@1.2-service disabled, so nothing starts it
# and every bootctl call fails with "Error getting bootctrl v1.0 module" -- a
# flashing script that switches slots then silently does nothing. This HAL talks
# to the GPT rather than a QSEE listener, so hwservicemanager is all it needs.
on property:hwservicemanager.ready=true
    start boot-hal-1-2

# get_number_slots() reports 3 because the QTI implementation counts by-name
# entries prefixed "boot" and TWRP adds a bare "boot" symlink. Cosmetic: slots,
# suffixes and flags all read back correctly and nothing uses the count.
